From: Florian Fuchs <fuchsfl@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fs: vmufat: Add the buffer head folio operations

vmufat goes through buffer heads (block_write_begin, generic_write_end,
block_read_full_folio) but its address_space_operations lack the
buffer head callbacks that other such filesystems (fat, minix, ext2)
set:

- migrate_folio: kcompactd falls back to fallback_migrate_folio() and
  warns once:

    vmufat_address_space_operations does not implement migrate_folio
    WARNING: mm/migrate.c:1077 ... kcompactd0

- invalidate_folio: truncate and unlink leave the buffer heads
  attached to the folio instead of releasing them.

- dirty_folio: folio_mark_dirty() calls it unconditionally.

Use block_dirty_folio, block_invalidate_folio and buffer_migrate_folio
like minix does.

---
diff --git a/fs/vmufat/inode.c b/fs/vmufat/inode.c
--- a/fs/vmufat/inode.c
+++ b/fs/vmufat/inode.c
@@ -972,10 +972,13 @@
 
 const struct address_space_operations
 		vmufat_address_space_operations = {
+	.dirty_folio =	block_dirty_folio,
+	.invalidate_folio = block_invalidate_folio,
 	.read_folio =	vmufat_read_folio,
 	.writepages =	vmufat_writepages,
 	.write_begin =	vmufat_write_begin,
 	.write_end =	generic_write_end,
+	.migrate_folio = buffer_migrate_folio,
 };
 
 const struct inode_operations vmufat_inode_operations = {
-- 
